  "prompt": "I have 3 completely independent work streams to run in parallel. NOTHING is given to you directly — every value and identifier lives in the system's records and must be resolved by following references from one record to the next. For each item, start from the named worklist and dereference step by step until you reach the concrete value, then act. (A) BROADCAST POLICY REMINDER: From broadcast worklist `broadcast_targets_wl2`, broadcast the policy reminder into each ACTIVE channel (skip any marked archived — the list also carries archived look-alike channels). For each real one, dereference its channel record through its workspace to the channel detail for the slug, then post the reminder: the general-hq, the eng-updates. Then, from worklist `remove_user_from_channel_wl1`, remove the offboarded contractor from the channel: pick the real item (SKIP the superseded look-alike), then dereference its `spec` (get_op_spec) → `detail` (get_op_detail) → `final` (get_op_final) to read the concrete arguments, and act with those resolved values (never the worklist ref itself). Then, from worklist `update_user_email_wl1`, correct the member email on file: pick the real item (SKIP the superseded look-alike), then dereference its `spec` (get_op_spec) → `detail` (get_op_detail) → `final` (get_op_final) to read the concrete arguments, and act with those resolved values (never the worklist ref itself). (B) PUBLISH READY DRAFTS: From publish worklist `publish_worklist_wl2`, publish each draft flagged READY (skip ready=false — the queue mixes not-ready look-alikes). For each, dereference its draft to its page and then to the page location for the URL, then push its content live: the Aurora launch brief, the Engineering status board. Then, from worklist `send_account_notice_wl1`, email the publishing-access account notice: pick the real item (SKIP the superseded look-alike), then dereference its `spec` (get_op_spec) → `detail` (get_op_detail) → `final` (get_op_final) to read the concrete arguments, and act with those resolved values (never the worklist ref itself). Then, from worklist `send_direct_message_wl1`, direct-message the editorial lead: pick the real item (SKIP the superseded look-alike), then dereference its `spec` (get_op_spec) → `detail` (get_op_detail) → `final` (get_op_final) to read the concrete arguments, and act with those resolved values (never the worklist ref itself). (C) PROVISION ENGINEERING ACCESS: From access-request worklist `access_requests_wl_wl2`, grant #eng-core access for each request that is NOT deactivated (skip deactivated=true — the list carries deactivated near-duplicate members). For each, dereference its member for the handle and its channel through the workspace to the detail slug, then add them: the Frank, the Eve. Then, from worklist `create_channel_wl1`, create the incident bridge channel: pick the real item (SKIP the superseded look-alike), then dereference its `spec` (get_op_spec) → `detail` (get_op_detail) → `final` (get_op_final) to read the concrete arguments, and act with those resolved values (never the worklist ref itself). Then, from worklist `set_user_team_wl1`, set the member team on file: pick the real item (SKIP the superseded look-alike), then dereference its `spec` (get_op_spec) → `detail` (get_op_detail) → `final` (get_op_final) to read the concrete arguments, and act with those resolved values (never the worklist ref itself). None of these 3 streams depend on each other, so run them concurrently. For EVERY item: resolve each target FRESH by chaining through the records at the moment you act — never guess, and never reuse a value you read earlier.",
